                      <td class="py-3 px-4">{fmtInt(row.w120)} W</td>
                      <td class="py-3 px-4 text-slate-500">{fmtInt(row.cont120)} W</td>
                      <td class="py-3 px-4">{fmtInt(row.w240)} W</td>
                      <td class="py-3 px-4 text-slate-500">{fmtInt(row.cont240)} W</td>
                    </tr>
                  ))
                }
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>

          <p class="mt-6 text-sm text-slate-500">
            Sources &amp; standards: NEC (NFPA 70) 2023 — 210.20(A) continuous load and the 125%/80%
            relationship, Article 100 definition of continuous load, 240.6(A) standard overcurrent ratings,
            Table 310.16 conductor ampacities. Local amendments override the model code, and a licensed
            electrician plus the AHJ have final say on anything installed.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <CalculatorFaqSection
